import lib/json_builders.dl

to get binary64 test bits of {a 64 bit floating-point number:value}:
    set copy to value
    return the value at ((the address of copy) as a pointer to a 64 bit unsigned integer)

to [check JSON decimal] {string:text} equals {a 64 bit floating-point number:expected}:
    parse text as JSON and set parsed to it
    require condition (parsed succeeded) reporting "A valid decimal was rejected"
    require condition ((binary64 test bits of (parsed's value's number)) = (binary64 test bits of expected)) reporting "Decimal parsing changed binary64 rounding"
    free parsed

to [check JSON float round trip of] {a 64 bit floating-point number:value}:
    set member to JSON number "value" is value
    set encoded to the compact JSON form of (member's value)
    parse encoded as JSON and set parsed to it
    require condition (parsed succeeded) reporting "A finite float produced invalid JSON"
    require condition ((binary64 test bits of (parsed's value's number)) = (binary64 test bits of value)) reporting "JSON serialization lost float precision or range"
    free parsed
    free member's value

check JSON decimal (the string form of "0.3") equals 0.3
check JSON decimal (the string form of "0.30000000000000004") equals (0.1 + 0.2)
check JSON decimal (the string form of "5e-324") equals 5e-324
check JSON decimal (the string form of "2.2250738585072014e-308") equals 2.2250738585072014e-308
check JSON decimal (the string form of "1.7976931348623157e308") equals 1.7976931348623157e308
check JSON decimal (the string form of "-0") equals (0.0 * -1.0)
set values to [0.0, 0.0 * -1.0, 0.1 + 0.2, ((6.0 - 0.18) - 0.18) - 0.18, 1e-7, -1e20, 1e308, 5e-324, 2.2250738585072014e-308, 1.7976931348623157e308]
set index to 0
loop while index < the length of values:
    check JSON float round trip of (the item at index in values)
    increment index
set member to JSON number "single" is (0.1 as a 32 bit floating-point number)
parse (member's value's text) as JSON and set parsed to it
require condition ((binary64 test bits of (parsed's value's number)) = (binary64 test bits of (member's value's number))) reporting "A float32 JSON builder lost its promoted value"
free parsed
free member's value
print line "JSON preserves binary64 rounding, signed zero, simulation arithmetic, subnormals and finite extremes."
